    character: "Robert Clive, a Company officer with more nerve than scruple. Siraj-ud-Daulah, the young Nawab of Bengal. Mir Jafar, the Nawab's own commander, who wanted his throne.",
    conflict: "The Nawab had seized Calcutta from the Company the year before. Clive retook it and then made a secret pact: if Mir Jafar kept his troops out of the fight, the Company would make him Nawab. The banker Jagat Seth, tired of Siraj, backed the plot.",
